WEBVTT

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:09.540
Young people spend a great deal of time online, yet many of them cannot tell true information from false.
年轻人花大量时间上网，然而他们当中许多人却分辨不出信息的真假。

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:18.120
They often believe sensational headlines, share unverified posts and fail to judge whether a website or an account is reliable.
他们常常轻信耸人听闻的标题，转发未经核实的帖子，也无法判断一个网站或账号是否可靠。

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:20.530
This phenomenon is worrying.
这一现象令人担忧。

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:28.570
False information can mislead young people in their daily decisions, from what products to buy to how to deal with health problems.
虚假信息会在日常决定中误导年轻人，从买什么产品到如何处理健康问题，无所不包。

00:00:29.370 --> 00:00:35.050
When they forward rumors without checking, they also help spread panic and confusion in society.
他们不加核实就转发谣言，也就助长了恐慌和混乱在社会上的蔓延。

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:45.470
The problem arises mainly because young people tend to trust whatever appears on their screens, and few of them have received training in evaluating information.
这个问题之所以出现，主要是因为年轻人往往相信屏幕上出现的一切，而他们当中很少有人接受过评估信息的训练。

00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:51.510
In addition, some websites deliberately create eye-catching but false stories for clicks.
此外，一些网站为了获得点击量，故意编造吸引眼球却虚假的故事。

00:00:52.310 --> 00:00:54.740
Several measures can help solve this problem.
有几项措施可以帮助解决这一问题。

00:00:55.540 --> 00:01:04.500
First, schools should offer courses on media literacy, teaching students how to check sources, compare reports and recognize the common tricks of fake news.
首先，学校应当开设媒介素养课程，教学生如何核查信息来源、对比报道，以及识别假新闻的常见伎俩。

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:12.650
Second, online platforms should monitor content more closely, label unverified posts and remove rumors promptly.
其次，网络平台应当更严格地监管内容，给未经核实的帖子加上标注，并及时删除谣言。

00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:19.730
Third, young people themselves should develop the habit of thinking twice before believing or sharing anything.
第三，年轻人自己应当养成习惯，在相信或转发任何信息之前三思。

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:27.940
If everyone does their part, young people can become wise users of the Internet rather than victims of false information.
只要每个人都尽到自己的责任，年轻人就能成为明智的网络使用者，而不是虚假信息的受害者。
